_🩺 Stability & Availability_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Do not truncate the exported PDF, and check the write result.**

`finish()` reopens `path` with `QIODevice::WriteOnly`, which truncates the existing valid PDF, then rewrites the full buffer. The return value of `out.write(data)` is never checked. If the write fails or is short (disk full, I/O error), the export leaves a truncated, unreadable PDF and the function still returns `true`.

An incremental update only needs the appended bytes, so open the file in append mode and verify the byte count.

<details>
<summary>🛡️ Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-        data += appended;
         QFile out(path);
-        if (!out.open(QIODevice::WriteOnly)) {
+        if (!out.open(QIODevice::WriteOnly | QIODevice::Append)) {
             if (errorOut)
                 *errorOut = QStringLiteral("Cannot rewrite PDF: ") + path;
             return false;
         }
-        out.write(data);
+        if (out.write(appended) != appended.size() || !out.flush()) {
+            if (errorOut)
+                *errorOut = QStringLiteral("Failed to append incremental update to PDF: ") + path;
+            return false;
+        }
+        data += appended;
         return true;
```
</details>

Note: with append mode, keep `newOffset` values computed from the original `data.size()`, which this code already does.

_🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Structure elements omit the required `/P` entry.**

PDF 32000-1 marks `/P` required for a structure element; it shall be an indirect reference to the immediate parent. The block elements (line 581), the per-page `/Part` elements (lines 593 and 604), and the `/Document` element (line 626) carry no `/P`, so the tree has no upward links. Strict validators, including PDF/UA checkers, reject that structure, which weakens the accessibility goal of this pass.

Object numbers are assigned sequentially, so add a reservation helper and fill `/P` while building each level.

<details>
<summary>♻️ Sketch: reserve the parent number before its children</summary>

```cpp
// in IncrementalUpdate
int reserveObj() { return nextObj++; }
void defineObj(int num, const QByteArray &body) { redefineObj(num, body); }
```

```cpp
const int partNum = u.reserveObj();
// children reference /P partNum 0 R
// ... then
u.defineObj(partNum, "<< /Type /StructElem /S /Part /P " + QByteArray::number(docElemNum)
                         + " 0 R /Pg " + QByteArray::number(pageObjNum) + " 0 R /K " + kidsArr + " >>");
```
</details>





