`1419-1429`: **🚀 Performance & Scalability** | **🔵 Trivial** | **⚡ Quick win**

**Build `modelToDisplay` in linear time.**

For each model offset, the inner loop scans `displayToModel` from index 0. The cost is O(M·D) per call. `blockTextLayout` runs in measurement, painting, caret, and hit-test, and it runs once for each laid fragment. Long paragraphs therefore become quadratic on hot paths. `displayToModel` is non-decreasing except for `-1` prefix entries, so a single forward pointer is enough.

<details>
<summary>♻️ Linear construction</summary>

```diff
-    for (int m = 0; m <= out.modelLength; ++m) {
-        int found = text.size();
-        for (int d = 0; d < out.displayToModel.size(); ++d) {
-            if (out.displayToModel.at(d) >= m) {
-                found = d;
-                break;
-            }
-        }
-        out.modelToDisplay[m] = found;
-    }
+    int d = 0;
+    for (int m = 0; m <= out.modelLength; ++m) {
+        while (d < out.displayToModel.size() && out.displayToModel.at(d) < m)
+            ++d;
+        out.modelToDisplay[m] = d < out.displayToModel.size() ? d : text.size();
+    }
```
</details>

Confirm that `displayToModel` stays monotonic after the hyphenation remap. The remap reuses `before[si]`, so the values should be monotonic.

**🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration** | **🟠 Major** | **⚡ Quick win**



**Skip native revision creation when embedded revisions are present.**

`document_save` embeds `aioffice.json` by default. `loadDocx` loads those revisions before parsing native markup. A format revision that spans multiple runs produces one native `w:rPrChange` per run. The importer then creates smaller native revisions. `flushP` removes only exact `blockId`, `kind`, `start`, and `end` matches, so the smaller revisions remain beside the JSON revision. Reopening the saved document therefore adds duplicate format revisions and breaks revision-count round trips.

When the embedded revision array is non-empty, skip native revision creation and preserve the JSON revision set.

<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
     const auto extraBytes = Zip::file(entries, QStringLiteral("word/aioffice.json"));
+    bool hasEmbeddedRevisions = false;
     if (!extraBytes.isEmpty()) {
         const auto extra = QJsonDocument::fromJson(extraBytes).object();
         doc.trackChanges = extra.value(QStringLiteral("track_changes")).toBool();
         for (const auto &b : extra.value(QStringLiteral("bookmarks")).toArray())
             doc.bookmarks.push_back(Bookmark::fromJson(b.toObject()));
-        for (const auto &r : extra.value(QStringLiteral("revisions")).toArray())
+        const auto embeddedRevisions = extra.value(QStringLiteral("revisions")).toArray();
+        hasEmbeddedRevisions = !embeddedRevisions.isEmpty();
+        for (const auto &r : embeddedRevisions)
             doc.revisions.push_back(Revision::fromJson(r.toObject()));
     }
```

```diff
     QVector<int> pendingRevisionIdx;
+    auto appendNativeRevision = [&](const Revision &rv) {
+        if (hasEmbeddedRevisions)
+            return;
+        doc.revisions.push_back(rv);
+        pendingRevisionIdx.push_back(doc.revisions.size() - 1);
+    };
```

Replace each native revision append in the format, insert, and delete branches with:

```diff
-                        doc.revisions.push_back(rv);
-                        pendingRevisionIdx.push_back(doc.revisions.size() - 1);
+                        appendNativeRevision(rv);
```

```diff
-                doc.revisions.push_back(rv);
-                pendingRevisionIdx.push_back(doc.revisions.size() - 1);
+                appendNativeRevision(rv);
```

</details>











✅ Addressed in commits 659da86 to 4776410

**🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration** | **🟡 Minor** | **⚡ Quick win**

**Record the format revision on the block whose prior runs were captured, and clamp the range.**

- The capture loop skips table blocks. It can therefore take `priorSlices` from `idx[k]`, a later block.
- Line 592 still sets `rev.blockId = doc_.body[idx.first()].id`.
- Trigger: `apply_character_format` with `ids: [tableId, paraId]` while track changes is on. The revision then points at the table, but `priorRuns` holds the paragraph's text.
- Consequence: `revision_reject` calls `restoreFormatPrior` on the table block. It writes the paragraph text into `table.runs` and does not restore the paragraph.
- Range problem: if `end` is past the block length, `splitRuns` clamps `priorSlices`, but `revEnd` keeps the unclamped `end`.
- Consequence: `restoreFormatPrior` computes `delta = newLen - oldLen != 0`. `shiftRevisionOffsets` then moves the other revisions in that block even though the text length did not change.

<details>
<summary>🐛 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
     QVector<TextRun> priorSlices;
     int revStart = start;
     int revEnd = end;
+    QString revBlockId;
     bool capturedPrior = false;
@@
         if (doc_.trackChanges && !capturedPrior && b.type != QLatin1String("table")) {
+            const int len = b.plainText().size();
             if (start >= 0 && end >= start) {
-                priorSlices = splitRuns(b.runs, start, end);
-                revStart = start;
-                revEnd = end;
+                revStart = qBound(0, start, len);
+                revEnd = qBound(revStart, end, len);
+                priorSlices = splitRuns(b.runs, revStart, revEnd);
             } else {
                 priorSlices = b.runs;
                 revStart = 0;
-                revEnd = 0;
-                for (const auto &r : b.runs)
-                    revEnd += r.text.size();
+                revEnd = len;
             }
+            revBlockId = b.id;
             capturedPrior = true;
         }
@@
-        rev.blockId = doc_.body[idx.first()].id;
+        rev.blockId = revBlockId.isEmpty() ? doc_.body[idx.first()].id : revBlockId;
```
</details>






