✅ Addressed in commits 215b5be to 67ab21c

**🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration** | **🟡 Minor** | **⚡ Quick win**



**Restrict native `IF` export to numeric and double-quoted operands.**

`singleComparison` accepts identifiers and single-quoted strings, then `nativeWordField` emits those tokens unchanged. Word does not resolve them from `doc.vars` or the page context. It may treat an identifier as a bookmark name or as text, so recalculating the field can select a different branch. The evaluator also removes single quotes, but the DOCX instruction preserves them; Word's string syntax uses double quotation marks.

When either operand is not numeric or double-quoted, use the evaluated-text fallback and preserve the field metadata:

<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
+bool wordIfOperandSafe(const QString &raw)
+{
+    if (raw.size() >= 2 && raw.front() == QLatin1Char('"') && raw.back() == QLatin1Char('"'))
+        return true;
+    bool ok = false;
+    raw.toDouble(&ok);
+    return ok;
+}
+
 // Native Word instruction, or false when the field must be the evaluated text.
 bool nativeWordField(const TextRun &r, DocxOut &o, QString &instr)
 {
     if (r.field == QLatin1String("if")) {
         const QJsonObject spec = fieldArgObject(r);
         if (!spec.value(QStringLiteral("cond")).isString())
             return false;
         QString left, op, right;
         if (!singleComparison(spec.value(QStringLiteral("cond")).toString(), left, op, right))
             return false;
+        if (!wordIfOperandSafe(left) || !wordIfOperandSafe(right))
+            return false;
         instr = QStringLiteral(" IF ") + left + QLatin1Char(' ') + wordCmpOp(op) + QLatin1Char(' ') + right
             + QLatin1Char(' ') + quoteFieldResult(spec.value(QStringLiteral("then")).toString())
             + QLatin1Char(' ') + quoteFieldResult(spec.value(QStringLiteral("else")).toString()) + QLatin1Char(' ');
         return true;
@@
         QString left, op, right;
         const QJsonObject spec = fieldArgObject(r);
         if (!spec.value(QStringLiteral("cond")).isString())
             return true;
-        return !singleComparison(spec.value(QStringLiteral("cond")).toString(), left, op, right);
+        return !singleComparison(spec.value(QStringLiteral("cond")).toString(), left, op, right)
+            || !wordIfOperandSafe(left) || !wordIfOperandSafe(right);
```

</details>











✅ Addressed in commits 215b5be to 67ab21c

**🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration** | **🟠 Major** | **🏗️ Heavy lift**

**Position-based `conditionals` restore can attach expressions to the wrong block or run.**

`rememberConditionals` records `{block: contentIndex, run: i}` from the model. `applyFieldConditionals` then writes `field`, `field_arg`, and `hide_if` into `doc.body[content[bi]].runs[ri]` with no identity check. The DOCX export/import cycle does not preserve these positions:
- **Block drift.** A `toc` block exports one `<w:p>` with `TOC1` style for each entry. The importer creates a `toc` block for each of those paragraphs. A TOC with N entries therefore shifts every later block index by N−1.
- **Run drift.** A run with `noteId` exports a text `<w:r>` and a separate reference `<w:r>`. The importer pushes both, so every later run index in that paragraph shifts by one. `revisedRunsToWml` also splits runs at revision boundaries. Empty runs without bold or italic are dropped on import.

The result is silent corruption on reopen with embedded JSON. An unrelated run can become a compound `if`, or the wrong paragraph can get `hide_if`. Verify identity before applying an entry. For example, store the exported visible text of the run and require a match. Apply `hide_if` only when the stored text of the block matches.

<details>
<summary>🛡️ Proposed guard (run entries)</summary>

```diff
         o.insert(QStringLiteral("field"), b.runs.at(i).field);
         o.insert(QStringLiteral("field_arg"), b.runs.at(i).fieldArg);
+        o.insert(QStringLiteral("shown"), runDisplayText(doc, b.runs.at(i)));
         out.append(o);
```

```diff
         const int ri = o.value(QStringLiteral("run")).toInt(-1);
-        if (ri < 0 || ri >= b.runs.size())
-            continue;
-        b.runs[ri].field = o.value(QStringLiteral("field")).toString();
-        b.runs[ri].fieldArg = o.value(QStringLiteral("field_arg")).toString();
+        const QString shown = o.value(QStringLiteral("shown")).toString();
+        int hit = -1;
+        for (int k = qMax(0, ri); k < b.runs.size() && hit < 0; ++k) {
+            if (b.runs[k].field.isEmpty() && b.runs[k].text == shown)
+                hit = k;
+        }
+        if (hit < 0)
+            continue;
+        b.runs[hit].field = o.value(QStringLiteral("field")).toString();
+        b.runs[hit].fieldArg = o.value(QStringLiteral("field_arg")).toString();
```

`rememberConditionals` needs a `const Document &` parameter for `runDisplayText`. Add a similar check for `hide_if`, for example a stored plain-text prefix of the block.
</details>





